WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:00.920
AJA HAMMERLY: In
this Cloud Minute,

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:02.628
I'm going to show you
how to enable cloud

00:00:02.628 --> 00:00:04.380
CDN for a backend service.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.799
Cloud CDN works as part
of cloud load balancing.

00:00:06.799 --> 00:00:09.340
I have a managed instance group
with a load balancer in front

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:11.750
of the instances already
set up in my project.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:14.870
I turn on cloud CDN and
navigate to Networking.

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.180
Then I click on Load
Balancing and click Edit

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.160
on my load balancer.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.250
Now I click Backend
Configuration,

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.720
click on my backend, and scroll
all the way to the bottom

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.150
and check the box
called Enable Cloud CDN.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:32.790
Now I click Update
to save the changes.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.090
Cloud CDN is enabled
and load balancing

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:37.430
will cache responses to
many requests at locations

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:38.302
all over the world.

00:00:38.302 --> 00:00:40.260
To find out more about
which types of responses

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:41.690
can be cached, you
can find a link

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:45.250
to the documentation in
the video description.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.870
I hope you found this
Cloud Minute helpful.

